WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.150
Kaze ni kami ga nabiku

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.150
My hair flows in the wind.

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:10.720
Kokoro ni hirogaru aozora no deai

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:10.720
An encounter in the blue skies of our hearts...

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:15.980
Tooku hanaretetemo

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:15.980
Though we are apart,

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:21.590
Kanjiru koto wa itsumo kimi dakara

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:21.590
I'm always thinking about you,

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:26.930
Itsu no hi ka mune wo hatte

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:26.930
so let's promise to meet again

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:32.410
Au koto wo yakusoku shiyou

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:32.410
one day, with our heads held high.

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:39.020
Zutto futari owari no nai

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:39.020
We'll be together, like a dream

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:45.410
Yume wo egaku you ni

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:45.410
with no end.

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:47.440
Kimi ni

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:47.440
I want

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:56.400
Kono omoi itsu no hi ka tsutaetai

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:56.400
to tell you this someday.

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:07.370
Sabishisa wo shiawase ni kaeru tame

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:07.370
I'm right here next to you

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:16.460
Soba ni iru yo kokoro wa

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:16.460
to turn your loneliness into joy.

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:24.830
Konna ni chikaku ni kanjiru

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:24.830
I can feel your heart so close to mine.

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:36.080
Episode 19 - A Mask Removed

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:40.280
I'm sorry. We're all sold out!

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:41.930
Oh no!

00:01:41.930 --> 00:01:44.630
But we're putting on an evening performance at eight o'clock tonight.

00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:49.080
The Stone's Smile

00:01:44.630 --> 00:01:49.090
I'll wait until later then; I have to give these flowers to Rei!

00:01:50.430 --> 00:01:52.840
It doesn't matter how long their line gets, there's no way...

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:55.720
they can match our theater.

00:01:55.720 --> 00:01:57.580
Take a look over there.

00:01:57.580 --> 00:01:58.770
Sir?

00:02:00.370 --> 00:02:02.160
Doesn't anything strike you as odd?

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:04.600
Well, there do seem to be more empty seats than usual.

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:06.640
More than that, the audience itself has changed.

00:02:06.980 --> 00:02:08.020
What do you mean?

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:09.590
Our regular audience has gone.

00:02:09.590 --> 00:02:12.170
Now, the audience consists of people involved in the show,

00:02:12.170 --> 00:02:14.590
friends of the cast, or die-hard fans.

00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:17.440
In other words, we are our own audience.

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:20.100
But that doesn't mean the audience has changed, does it?

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:24.090
We normally have more theatergoers.

00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:28.340
It's very important to attract the kind of audience that demands entertainment,

00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:30.450
enjoyment and a spectacle.

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:34.590
Over there, they'll put on any show as long as it's entertaining.

00:02:34.590 --> 00:02:37.910
Theatergoers are thus entertained and impressed,

00:02:37.910 --> 00:02:40.080
so they keep coming back.

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:42.260
You can't make a name for yourself in show business if you can't capture...

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:43.690
the hearts of the masses!

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:46.150
The problem is: what do we do now?

00:02:46.150 --> 00:02:50.620
Thinking about the future is more and more uncertain.

00:02:50.830 --> 00:02:53.120
I want to know more about you, Pio.

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:55.350
About me? Okay, Hannah.

00:02:55.350 --> 00:02:58.350
I don't believe it. The place was empty on the opening night!

00:02:58.350 --> 00:03:02.400
Then, come with me. The sky's the limit!

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:04.180
Rei sure is popular.

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:05.890
Oh, he's here again.

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:09.940
Ryou Majima - he's the guy who played Maya's love interest in <i>Wuthering Heights</i>.

00:03:09.940 --> 00:03:11.480
He comes to every show!

00:03:11.480 --> 00:03:14.840
That reminds me... Maya's friend, Sakurakouji...

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:16.390
He hasn't even come to one of our shows yet.

00:03:16.390 --> 00:03:19.310
He used to turn up to watch Maya's shows...

00:03:19.310 --> 00:03:23.030
What about that guy over there? He's also been here before, hasn't he?

00:03:23.810 --> 00:03:28.000
But Maya's doing pretty well. She's been playing a doll for ten days now,

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:29.610
but she's hanging in there.

00:03:29.610 --> 00:03:32.850
That's right. This whole show relies on Maya.

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:34.860
Ms. Tsukikage?

00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:37.340
Are you feeling all right?

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:41.300
Yes, I've been given permission to leave the hospital for the day.

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:45.060
I'm not exaggerating when I say that the whole play...

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:49.280
rides on Maya's performance as the doll.

00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:52.890
If Maya displays even the faintest trace of human emotion,

00:03:52.890 --> 00:03:55.550
everything would fall apart.

00:03:56.410 --> 00:04:00.680
You could say this show is marked by this high-wire act.

00:04:04.020 --> 00:04:06.860
These are the candidates for the role of Helen.

00:04:06.860 --> 00:04:12.320
For the starring role of Helen Keller in the Daito Theater's season opener,

00:04:12.320 --> 00:04:16.330
we have combed through a vast pool of stars and potential actresses,

00:04:16.330 --> 00:04:18.290
and have narrowed our decision down to these fifteen.

00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:21.100
Excuse me, but there's one more potential candidate.

00:04:22.080 --> 00:04:24.730
I stumbled upon her in that basement theater.

00:04:24.730 --> 00:04:25.790
What kind of actress is she?

00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:29.390
In the show, she plays the role of a doll and doesn't move an inch.

00:04:29.390 --> 00:04:36.510
Hm... she doesn't speak or move, yet from that role alone, you believe she's talented?

00:04:36.510 --> 00:04:39.310
Yes, she has no lines and doesn't move at all.

00:04:39.310 --> 00:04:41.500
But that's exactly the nature of a doll.

00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:44.910
She plays the role to the point that you think she might not even be human.

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:54.720
We'd like to join your troupe!

00:04:54.720 --> 00:04:57.350
Okay... will you come for an audition then?

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:02.240
Majima!

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:03.300
It's been a while, hasn't it?

00:05:03.510 --> 00:05:04.690
Yeah.

00:05:05.970 --> 00:05:08.250
Yeah, Heathcliff!

00:05:08.910 --> 00:05:10.420
Cathy...

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:14.420
Wow, I've never been to such a fancy place before!

00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:19.190
Sorry! I must be embarrassing you...

00:05:19.190 --> 00:05:21.930
Not at all! I'm glad you came.

00:05:22.260 --> 00:05:26.720
But you're so popular, and you have so many female fans.

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:28.960
It just looks that way.

00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:31.960
You know, I'm also a fan of a lot of actors too.

00:05:32.510 --> 00:05:34.400
I've been coming to see you every day.

00:05:35.590 --> 00:05:38.770
Will you go out with me?

00:05:47.340 --> 00:05:49.590
When I saw you on stage as Cathy, it felt like my perfect girl...

00:05:49.590 --> 00:05:52.700
was standing right there in front of me.

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:55.970
You're different from any girl I've ever met before.

00:05:55.970 --> 00:05:59.580
I could feel your kindness and the fierceness of your affection...

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:01.140
and I was completely taken in by your Cathy.

00:06:01.140 --> 00:06:06.320
Um, I'm actually a pretty boring girl who can't do anything right!

00:06:06.320 --> 00:06:08.430
I'm not like Cathy at all!

00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:12.830
Not like Cathy at all. Of course.

00:06:12.830 --> 00:06:16.920
It was stupid of me to carry on like this, when all I desire is the illusion of Cathy.

00:06:18.630 --> 00:06:21.090
Do you have someone you like?

00:06:21.540 --> 00:06:22.740
Yeah.

00:06:23.810 --> 00:06:26.630
All right then. I guess I'll have to deal with being rejected.

00:06:26.630 --> 00:06:27.790
I'm so sorry!

00:06:27.790 --> 00:06:29.330
So? What kind of person is he?

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:34.600
He's very kind and always looks out for me...

00:06:35.400 --> 00:06:37.670
And are you in love?

00:06:38.820 --> 00:06:39.850
In love?

00:06:42.420 --> 00:06:45.500
The next time we meet, it will be as good friends.

00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:46.980
Like we've been until now.

00:06:46.980 --> 00:06:49.410
Yeah. Good bye then.

00:06:49.410 --> 00:06:50.500
Maya.

00:06:50.870 --> 00:06:54.510
I was really happy when we were performing <i>Wuthering Heights</i>.

00:06:57.480 --> 00:06:58.790
Thank you.

00:06:59.770 --> 00:07:01.760
Good bye, Cathy.

00:07:05.710 --> 00:07:08.020
I'm so sorry, Majima!

00:07:08.020 --> 00:07:10.070
It's a shame. He's such a nice guy.

00:07:17.020 --> 00:07:21.510
Sakurakouji. Why haven't you come to see our show yet?

00:07:22.520 --> 00:07:25.470
There are so many things I want to talk to you about!

00:07:27.750 --> 00:07:30.330
Today's the final performance! Let's make it our best yet!

00:07:31.750 --> 00:07:32.600
Maya!

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:34.470
Sumiko?

00:07:34.890 --> 00:07:37.680
Good. I've been looking for you!

00:07:38.090 --> 00:07:38.900
Maya?

00:07:38.900 --> 00:07:41.040
Oh, this is Sumiko!

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:43.660
She's the daughter of the restaurant owners I used to work for in Yokohama.

00:07:43.660 --> 00:07:46.660
My mother and I lived there.

00:07:46.950 --> 00:07:49.290
How's my mom doing?

00:07:49.290 --> 00:07:51.670
Is she still mad at me for running away?

00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:54.900
I guess you haven't heard yet.

00:07:54.900 --> 00:07:57.180
Maya, brace yourself.

00:07:59.730 --> 00:08:03.480
You're telling me that my mom checked into a health clinic in Yamanashi?!

00:08:04.320 --> 00:08:07.510
Yeah, but we got a call from them this morning...

00:08:07.510 --> 00:08:10.470
They told us she disappeared three days ago.

00:08:11.520 --> 00:08:13.950
As you can imagine, we're really worried too...

00:08:13.950 --> 00:08:16.290
Maya, do you have any idea where she could have gone?

00:08:16.940 --> 00:08:20.050
Mom. She doesn't have anywhere else to go...

00:08:20.050 --> 00:08:21.810
I can't think of anywhere!

00:08:24.260 --> 00:08:25.260
Maya, we have to hurry...

00:08:26.070 --> 00:08:30.470
Rei! I was worried, so I decided to come and pick you up.

00:08:30.470 --> 00:08:32.870
Sorry, we caught a later bus.

00:08:32.870 --> 00:08:34.820
Maya, you have to pull yourself together!

00:08:51.840 --> 00:08:53.030
Mom!

00:08:52.430 --> 00:08:55.010
Maya! Watch out!

00:08:56.550 --> 00:08:57.740
Mom!

00:08:59.660 --> 00:09:01.500
Mom!

00:09:04.220 --> 00:09:06.190
Where are you going, Maya?

00:09:06.190 --> 00:09:07.350
We have a show to perform!

00:09:09.790 --> 00:09:12.390
The doors open in fifteen minutes, you know.

00:09:14.060 --> 00:09:15.510
Open...

00:09:16.910 --> 00:09:19.440
We've finally made it to our final show.

00:09:19.440 --> 00:09:22.480
So, let's make sure we don't let all our hard work go to waste.

00:09:23.420 --> 00:09:26.500
Mom... you looked so exhausted...

00:09:29.910 --> 00:09:33.720
The entire fortune of the Bartholomew family?!

00:09:34.480 --> 00:09:36.210
I'll carry some too!

00:09:36.210 --> 00:09:38.800
Sure you can. Maybe when you're a bit bigger.

00:09:39.050 --> 00:09:41.310
It's just not fair!

00:09:41.880 --> 00:09:44.390
Here, you can have my portion too.

00:09:44.650 --> 00:09:46.720
What can I do for a doll?

00:09:47.390 --> 00:09:51.310
You look good. To think that you're in middle school now!

00:09:51.770 --> 00:09:54.730
Mom... I'm sorry. I'm so sorry.

00:09:54.730 --> 00:09:55.900
Well, well...

00:09:55.900 --> 00:10:00.490
Mom, I've ignored you for so long.

00:10:01.400 --> 00:10:04.460
When I'm the only person you have!

00:10:04.850 --> 00:10:05.650
Hey!

00:10:05.650 --> 00:10:06.990
Wait a minute.

00:10:06.990 --> 00:10:08.070
But that's...

00:10:20.220 --> 00:10:25.100
Her doll's mask has fallen off.

00:10:42.070 --> 00:10:45.700
Her mask has fallen off! Maya!

00:10:55.090 --> 00:10:57.950
Oh no, I slipped.

00:10:56.840 --> 00:10:59.550
Oh no! How could I do that on stage?!

00:10:59.550 --> 00:11:01.140
My precious Elizabeth is soaked!

00:11:01.500 --> 00:11:02.390
Hannah...

00:11:02.390 --> 00:11:03.150
Yes, sir?

00:11:03.150 --> 00:11:04.990
Please change Elizabeth.

00:11:04.990 --> 00:11:06.300
Yes, sir.

00:11:10.580 --> 00:11:11.840
Maya...

00:11:11.840 --> 00:11:14.850
I will not need you for our next play..

00:11:14.850 --> 00:11:17.810
For the time being, you are on probation.

00:11:18.350 --> 00:11:19.770
Probation?

00:11:19.770 --> 00:11:21.600
Ma'am!

00:11:21.600 --> 00:11:25.430
If it wasn't for Rei's quick thinking, the whole play would have turned into a fiasco!

00:11:25.430 --> 00:11:29.090
Maya... the stage doesn't belong to one person.

00:11:29.090 --> 00:11:34.030
Actors are all individual stones supporting the walls of a castle.

00:11:34.030 --> 00:11:37.980
If one of those stones becomes loose, the castle collapses!

00:11:38.410 --> 00:11:40.680
A stone in a wall.

00:11:41.120 --> 00:11:44.700
When you took your mask off on stage,

00:11:44.890 --> 00:11:48.410
you stopped being an actor.

00:11:50.380 --> 00:11:53.350
Stopped being an actor?

00:11:54.430 --> 00:11:56.570
You say you saw your mother?

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:05.090
Actors are never allowed to let their masks slip...

00:12:05.360 --> 00:12:11.710
No matter how sad you are nor how hard your own life is, that sadness is your own.

00:12:11.710 --> 00:12:13.820
It has nothing to do with your character.

00:12:14.470 --> 00:12:18.850
Before you start acting, you need to smother your real self.

00:12:19.200 --> 00:12:21.200
Acting is about glass masks.

00:12:21.200 --> 00:12:23.410
Glass masks?

00:12:24.480 --> 00:12:29.510
All of us wear fragile glass masks when we perform.

00:12:29.940 --> 00:12:34.330
No matter how thoroughly you throw yourself into your character,

00:12:34.330 --> 00:12:37.670
the mask can still break very easily, revealing your true face.

00:12:38.090 --> 00:12:43.460
The skill of an actor solely relies on how long...

00:12:43.460 --> 00:12:47.500
they can wear their glass mask.

00:12:55.650 --> 00:12:59.480
Get up, Maya! Maya!

00:12:59.480 --> 00:13:01.290
Maya?

00:13:07.300 --> 00:13:11.060
Where did you go, Mom?

00:13:11.420 --> 00:13:14.920
You've nowhere else to go...

00:13:15.410 --> 00:13:16.810
Mom!

00:13:23.630 --> 00:13:25.560
You're looking for your mother?

00:13:26.020 --> 00:13:28.570
You're just wandering aimlessly around Tokyo,

00:13:28.570 --> 00:13:31.890
hoping you'll find her? You've only got a one in a million chance!

00:13:31.890 --> 00:13:35.690
But there's still a chance, no matter how small!

00:13:35.690 --> 00:13:37.780
I'm gonna take my chances!

00:13:37.780 --> 00:13:42.790
I can't just stand by and do nothing, if there's even the slightest of chances!

00:13:45.110 --> 00:13:46.260
Mom...

00:13:49.170 --> 00:13:50.280
Mom!

00:13:51.490 --> 00:13:55.830
Your casting for <i>Muenzakura</i> is perfect!

00:13:55.830 --> 00:13:58.660
Just what I'd expect from the Daito Theater, President Hayami!

00:13:58.660 --> 00:13:59.620
Thank you very much.

00:13:59.620 --> 00:14:03.590
And Ayumi Himekawa's playing the cool little young lady of the family...

00:14:03.590 --> 00:14:06.180
Her reputation is even envied by veteran actors!

00:14:06.430 --> 00:14:08.510
Her looks, her presence -

00:14:08.510 --> 00:14:12.940
that girl was born a leading lady.

00:14:13.250 --> 00:14:15.290
Find her right away!

00:14:15.290 --> 00:14:16.390
Yes, sir!

00:14:16.390 --> 00:14:20.360
I want you to find a girl who's attended the rehearsals...

00:14:20.360 --> 00:14:22.470
and remembers all the lines. Preferably, a girl in her teens.

00:14:22.470 --> 00:14:24.830
Is something wrong, Mr. Kikuchi?

00:14:24.830 --> 00:14:28.380
Yes. One of our actresses has been involved in an accident.

00:14:28.760 --> 00:14:30.050
Are you serious?

00:14:30.050 --> 00:14:32.730
She's not badly injured, but we need to find another actress...

00:14:32.730 --> 00:14:35.200
for the role immediately!

00:14:40.840 --> 00:14:42.600
Mom...

00:14:42.600 --> 00:14:43.940
What are you doing here?

00:14:43.940 --> 00:14:45.590
Sheltering from the rain?

00:14:46.050 --> 00:14:49.300
Mr. Hayami! Please leave me alone.

00:14:49.300 --> 00:14:50.550
I need to speak to you.

00:14:51.020 --> 00:14:52.160
Let me go!

00:14:52.160 --> 00:14:53.170
It concerns acting!

00:14:55.960 --> 00:14:58.350
This is an official request.

00:14:59.280 --> 00:15:00.990
Miss Maya Kitajima.

00:15:03.110 --> 00:15:06.080
About that role, Masumi...

00:15:06.080 --> 00:15:09.420
Mr. Kikuchi, I've found someone to fill in for you.

00:15:09.780 --> 00:15:11.530
This girl?

00:15:11.530 --> 00:15:14.470
Yes. She's no ordinary actress, you know.

00:15:14.590 --> 00:15:16.340
But I don't even...

00:15:16.340 --> 00:15:19.640
You said you wanted some part-time work, didn't you?

00:15:19.640 --> 00:15:21.170
This will be perfect for you.

00:15:21.730 --> 00:15:24.300
I don't think you want to refuse this opportunity over something...

00:15:24.300 --> 00:15:27.190
as petty as your personal grudge against me.

00:15:27.190 --> 00:15:34.540
And it's possible your one and only fan will come and see the show.

00:15:34.540 --> 00:15:36.950
Mr. or Mrs. Purple Rose...

00:15:36.950 --> 00:15:41.050
That's right. They always seem to attend the bigger venues...

00:15:48.730 --> 00:15:50.640
Step right in.

00:15:53.400 --> 00:15:55.760
Ah, Ayumi!

00:15:59.000 --> 00:16:00.550
Ayumi!

00:16:00.550 --> 00:16:03.710
This is the girl we've drafted in to play your cousin, Chie. Her name...

00:16:03.710 --> 00:16:05.030
is Maya Kitajima.

00:16:05.560 --> 00:16:07.380
She's playing my cousin?

00:16:07.380 --> 00:16:09.450
I'm looking forward to working with you.

00:16:09.660 --> 00:16:13.000
I see. This will be our first time on stage together.

00:16:13.000 --> 00:16:14.440
Let's do our best.

00:16:14.680 --> 00:16:17.400
I'll be acting on stage with Ayumi...

00:16:18.580 --> 00:16:21.040
That's right. We don't have a lot of time before the curtain goes up.

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:26.170
This show, <i>Muenzakura</i>, is a story about the ups and downs of Baron Kaidouji's family...

00:16:26.170 --> 00:16:30.180
during the glorious times of the Rokumeikan.

00:16:30.180 --> 00:16:33.080
Ayumi is the Baron's granddaughter.

00:16:33.080 --> 00:16:35.720
Chie, the girl you'll be playing, is the offspring of a union...

00:16:35.720 --> 00:16:38.960
between the Baron's prodigal fifth son, Yukihiro, and a geisha.

00:16:39.340 --> 00:16:42.980
Your character has lived with her shame since early childhood.

00:16:42.980 --> 00:16:46.000
You are needed in scenes three and four of the first act.

00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:49.600
In Act Two, you'll be in the fifth scene.

00:16:49.930 --> 00:16:52.520
The show starts at six thirty, so you have forty-five minutes to prepare.

00:16:52.770 --> 00:16:55.180
You're telling me she's going to learn all of her lines...

00:16:55.180 --> 00:16:56.500
in forty-five minutes? Who exactly is this girl?!

00:17:02.170 --> 00:17:03.650
Look at her!

00:17:04.260 --> 00:17:06.760
What concentration!

00:17:10.680 --> 00:17:13.230
The doors are now open!

00:17:13.970 --> 00:17:16.580
Do you know that they call her "The Stage Storm"?

00:17:16.580 --> 00:17:19.630
But we're sharing a scene with her!

00:17:19.630 --> 00:17:21.350
What if she steals our scene?

00:17:21.350 --> 00:17:25.360
We'll just have to make sure we strike first!

00:17:26.490 --> 00:17:30.350
"The bowl's in the cupboard."

00:17:29.250 --> 00:17:30.360
Miss Kitajima?

00:17:30.350 --> 00:17:32.030
No, that's not right...

00:17:30.940 --> 00:17:32.430
Miss Maya Kitajima?

00:17:32.430 --> 00:17:33.810
Miss Kitajima!

00:17:33.810 --> 00:17:37.670
It's time to get into costume and sort out your makeup!

00:17:37.670 --> 00:17:39.210
Here, I'll help you.

00:17:39.210 --> 00:17:41.000
Come on! Hurry!

00:17:39.350 --> 00:17:40.290
But...

00:17:49.360 --> 00:17:54.100
Grandfather! Look, Grandfather!

00:17:54.100 --> 00:17:57.150
Today, I learned the Western way of introducing myself!

00:18:01.500 --> 00:18:04.240
You bend your back like this...

00:18:01.680 --> 00:18:04.220
She's so pretty!

00:18:04.640 --> 00:18:09.500
My first scene is in the kitchen. Even though I'm the daughter of a nobleman,

00:18:09.500 --> 00:18:13.230
I'm mistaken for a servant.

00:18:14.110 --> 00:18:17.220
I'll do it! My Chie!

00:18:19.270 --> 00:18:20.230
Hey, maid!

00:18:20.230 --> 00:18:25.160
If there's any rice left over, can you make some riceballs for me?

00:18:25.160 --> 00:18:27.770
If you want rice, there's some in the pot.

00:18:28.870 --> 00:18:34.550
How can she stay so calm when she's not even been to a single rehearsal?

00:18:35.260 --> 00:18:38.560
Thanks! Then I'll go ahead and take some.

00:18:39.430 --> 00:18:41.230
Can you wait till I'm done please?

00:18:45.630 --> 00:18:49.770
Who d'you think you are, anyways?!

00:18:50.290 --> 00:18:53.810
Oh balls! I just slipped into my Tokyo dialect...

00:18:54.940 --> 00:18:58.550
You don't like the thought of me eating with you?

00:19:12.270 --> 00:19:14.540
Has she forgotten her line?

00:19:14.540 --> 00:19:15.700
Shh.

00:19:20.880 --> 00:19:27.430
I'm sorry. It's just that I'm so used to eating alone.

00:19:28.100 --> 00:19:30.140
You mean you're part of the household?!

00:19:29.250 --> 00:19:31.700
She deliberately paused there.

00:19:31.700 --> 00:19:34.030
Aren't you over-analyzing, Ayumi?

00:19:34.030 --> 00:19:35.170
She's had no rehearsals and she's only just learned her lines.

00:19:35.170 --> 00:19:37.570
I doubt any normal human being would have the time...

00:19:37.570 --> 00:19:39.220
to think of anything as calculated as that...

00:19:40.390 --> 00:19:43.330
That girl? A normal human being?

00:19:43.880 --> 00:19:46.830
When she steps on stage, she becomes a totally different person.

00:19:46.830 --> 00:19:50.430
What's frightening is that it <i>isn't</i> calculated, but instinctual.

00:19:50.690 --> 00:19:56.190
At first sight, she may not seem like much, but then, she starts to radiate.

00:19:56.190 --> 00:19:59.040
Look! He's perfect proof of that!

00:19:59.040 --> 00:20:02.010
He's slowly starting to crumble.

00:20:02.800 --> 00:20:07.180
That's why she's called "The Stage Storm."

00:20:10.590 --> 00:20:12.720
We'll finish her off in the next scene.

00:20:12.720 --> 00:20:16.240
Soon. I'm on soon.

00:20:16.240 --> 00:20:19.130
Master! Oh, this is terrible! Master Yukihiro has...

00:20:19.130 --> 00:20:23.250
What's the meaning of this? What exactly has Yukihiro done?!

00:20:23.250 --> 00:20:25.920
Please, look at this!

00:20:29.230 --> 00:20:31.430
What's wrong, little one? You're shaking!

00:20:31.430 --> 00:20:32.590
It's wrong...

00:20:32.590 --> 00:20:33.410
What?

00:20:33.410 --> 00:20:36.970
The script doesn't match up with this scene!

00:20:36.970 --> 00:20:38.140
What do you mean?

00:20:38.550 --> 00:20:43.670
In the script I have, it says that I come on when Yukihiro returns...

00:20:44.040 --> 00:20:48.190
What?! That's from the script <i>before</i> we rewrote this scene!

00:20:48.520 --> 00:20:50.430
Someone's switched your script!

00:20:50.430 --> 00:20:52.170
Why would someone do this?!

00:20:54.020 --> 00:20:56.190
Chie is supposed to go on at any moment!

00:20:56.190 --> 00:21:00.200
Chie might know. Chie! Come over here!

00:21:00.510 --> 00:21:03.660
You can't go on like this! We have to stop her from going on!

00:21:03.660 --> 00:21:05.940
Can anyone else step into this scene?

00:21:05.940 --> 00:21:09.650
But if Chie doesn't go on stage, we can't progress to the next scene!

00:21:09.650 --> 00:21:11.300
<i>Chie</i>!

00:21:11.300 --> 00:21:12.180
I'm on!

00:21:12.660 --> 00:21:13.980
Little one.

00:21:15.570 --> 00:21:17.540
Hey, little one! Wait!

00:21:17.540 --> 00:21:20.450
Aren't you embarrassed, Masumi?

00:21:20.450 --> 00:21:23.100
You're losing your cool. That's not like you.

00:21:23.610 --> 00:21:25.940
Miss Mizuki. But...

00:21:25.940 --> 00:21:29.100
She's gone on stage because she's been called.

00:21:29.780 --> 00:21:33.290
Once a show starts, it must go on.

00:21:33.290 --> 00:21:35.840
Shouldn't you know that better than anyone else?

00:21:36.810 --> 00:21:42.570
Without knowing her lines, Maya has walked out on stage.

00:21:42.570 --> 00:21:46.510
It was such an incredibly reckless act that...

00:21:46.510 --> 00:21:49.800
even the calm and clear-headed Masumi Hayami has been thrown into a frenzy.

00:22:08.640 --> 00:22:15.370
Asa kara yoru made yoru kara asa made

00:22:08.640 --> 00:22:15.370
From morning until night, from dusk till dawn,

00:22:15.910 --> 00:22:23.310
Futari ai no ondo wo itsumo kanjiru desho

00:22:15.910 --> 00:22:23.310
you can feel the warmth of our love.

00:22:23.310 --> 00:22:30.000
Shunkashuutou mo ippun ichibyou mo

00:22:23.310 --> 00:22:30.000
All year round, every minute and every second,

00:22:30.830 --> 00:22:37.940
Futari hada no ondo wo itsumo kanjiru desho

00:22:30.830 --> 00:22:37.940
you can feel the warmth of our skin.

00:22:38.640 --> 00:22:46.190
Kono dokidoki wa makka ni moeru taiyou

00:22:38.640 --> 00:22:46.190
This excitement is burning brightly like the sun,

00:22:46.190 --> 00:22:51.480
Atsuku moete atsuku togashite

00:22:46.190 --> 00:22:51.480
let us burn brightly, let us burn until we're hot

00:22:51.480 --> 00:22:56.290
Koi wo shimashou!

00:22:51.480 --> 00:22:56.290
and make love!

00:22:56.600 --> 00:22:58.990
It's so Make it Make it Naked!

00:22:56.600 --> 00:22:58.990
It's so Make it Make it Naked!

00:22:58.990 --> 00:23:00.760
Make it Make it Naked!

00:22:58.990 --> 00:23:00.760
Make it Make it Naked!

00:23:00.760 --> 00:23:04.070
Sunao na mama dakiaou!

00:23:00.760 --> 00:23:04.070
Let's hold and be true to each other!

00:23:04.070 --> 00:23:10.570
Isso mekimeki nekki! mekimeki daisuki!

00:23:04.070 --> 00:23:10.570
And let's add more heat! I love the heat!

00:23:10.570 --> 00:23:13.960
Aishiae!

00:23:10.570 --> 00:23:13.960
Feel the love!

00:23:21.990 --> 00:23:25.930
Maya, I thought I told you that you were on probation,

00:23:25.930 --> 00:23:29.020
so why did you perform in <i>Muenzakura</i>?

00:23:29.760 --> 00:23:33.820
Well, perhaps it did you some good to be exposed to the raw talent...

00:23:33.820 --> 00:23:35.890
of Ayumi Himekawa.

00:23:36.330 --> 00:23:40.680
But you can't run away because you're afraid of her.

00:23:40.680 --> 00:23:43.930
If you run away now, you can forget about learning anything from me!

00:23:43.930 --> 00:23:47.920
If you don't want that to happen, go and win the role of Helen Keller over Ayumi.

00:23:47.920 --> 00:23:50.990
You need to grow stronger, Maya!

00:23:47.950 --> 00:23:51.580
Episode 20 - The Switched Script
